Crawled: last month; OmniVLA: Unifiying Multi-Sensor Perception for Physically-Grounded Multimodal VLA ... November 2025\nThis enables iterative reflection and globally informed planning, reframing research as a progressive process. Empirical results show that Re-TRAC consistently outperforms ReAct by 15-20% on BrowseComp with frontier LLMs. For smaller models, we introduce Re-TRAC-aware supervised fine-tuning, achieving state-of-the-art performance at comparable scales. Notably, Re-TRAC shows a monotonic reduction in tool calls and token usage across rounds, indicating progressively targeted exploration driven by cross-trajectory reflection rather than redundant search.\n\nOmniVLA: Unifiying Multi-Sensor Perception for Physically-Grounded Multimodal VLA\n\nPreprint\n\nFile available\n\nNovember 2025\n\n·\n\n58 Reads\n\nHeyu Guo\n\n·\n\nShanmu Wang\n\n·\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n·\n\n[...]\n\n·\n\nLili Qi\n\nVision-language-action (VLA) models have shown strong generalization for action prediction through large-scale vision-language pretraining. However, most existing models rely solely on RGB cameras, limiting their perception and, consequently, manipulation capabilities. We present OmniVLA, an omni-modality VLA model that integrates novel sensing modalities for physically-grounded spatial intelligence beyond RGB perception. The core of our approach is the sensor-masked image, a unified representation that overlays spatially grounded and physically meaningful masks onto the RGB images, derived from sensors including an infrared camera, a mmWave radar, and a microphone array. This image-native unification keeps sensor input close to RGB statistics to facilitate training, provides a uniform interface across sensor hardware, and enables data-efficient learning with lightweight per-sensor projectors. Built on this, we present a multisensory vision-language-action model architecture and train the model based on an RGB-pretrained VLA backbone. We evaluate OmniVLA on challenging real-world tasks where sensor-modality perception is needed to guide the manipulation. OmniVLA achieves an average task success rate of 84%, significantly outperforms both RGB-only and raw-sensor-input baseline models by 59% and 28% respectively, meanwhile showing higher learning efficiency and stronger generalization capability.\n\n[Button: Read more]\n\nDownload\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRuichun Ma (https://www.csauthors.net/ruichun-ma/)\nciteturn4658search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Netw., December, 2025OmniVLA: Physically-Grounded Multimodal VLA with Unified Multi-Sensor Perception for Robotic Manipulation. ... CoRR, November, 2025\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n,\n\nWenjun Hu\n\nIEEE Trans. Netw., December, 2025\n\nOmniVLA: Physically-Grounded Multimodal VLA with Unified Multi-Sensor Perception for Robotic Manipulation.\n\n[BibT_{e}X]\n\n[DOI]\n\nHeyu Guo\n\n,\n\nShanmu Wang\n\n,\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n,\n\nShiqi Jiang\n\n,\n\nYasaman Ghasempour\n\n,\n\nOmid Abari\n\n,\n\nBaining Guo\n\n,\n\nLili Qiu\n\nCoRR, November, 2025\n\nmmET: mmWave Radar-Based Eye Tracking on Smart Glasses.\n\n[BibT_{e}X]\n\n[DOI]\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n,\n\nYasuo Morimoto\n\n,\n\nJohn S. Ho\n\n,\n\nSam Shiu\n\n,\n\nJiang Zhu\n\nProceedings of the 23rd ACM Conference on Embedded Networked Sensor Systems, 2025\n\nCGMM: Non-Invasive Continuous Glucose Monitoring in Wearables Using Metasurfaces.\n\n[BibT_{e}X]\n\n[DOI]\n\nHao Pan\n\n,\n\nYezhou Wang\n\n,\n\nJiting Liu\n\n,\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n,\n\nLili Qiu\n\n,\n\nYi-Chao Chen\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTransformer Cuántico Híbrido para Generación de Lenguaje | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/es/overview/2511.10653)\nciteturn4658search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; November 2, 2025 ... Investigadores de la Universidad de Nankai desarrollaron HyQuT, el primer modelo de lenguaje grande híbrido cuántico-clásico, integrando circuitos cuánticos variacionales en arquitecturas Transformer para la generación de lenguaje natural.\n\nTransformer Cuántico Híbrido para Generación de Lenguaje\n\nNovember 2, 2025\n\nCopy Markdown\n\nDesheng Kong, Xiangshuo Cui, Jiaying Jin, Jing Xu, Donglin Wang\n\n### Resumen IA\n\nInvestigadores de la Universidad de Nankai desarrollaron HyQuT, el primer modelo de lenguaje grande híbrido cuántico-clásico, integrando circuitos cuánticos variacionales en arquitecturas Transformer para la generación de lenguaje natural. Este enfoque redujo los parámetros clásicos en más del 10% en modelos de hasta 150 millones de parámetros, manteniendo una capacitación estable y una generación de texto coherente.\n\nInvestigadores de la Universidad de Nankai desarrollaron HyQuT, el primer modelo de lenguaje grande híbrido cuántico-clásico, integrando circuitos cuánticos variacionales en arquitecturas Transformer para la generación de lenguaje natural. Este enfoque redujo los parámetros clásicos en más del 10% en modelos de hasta 150 millones de parámetros, manteniendo una capacitación estable y una generación de texto coherente.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nहाइब्रिड क्वांटम ट्रांसफॉर्मर भाषा निर्माण के लिए | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/hi/overview/2511.10653)\nciteturn4658search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; November 2, 2025 ... नानकाई विश्वविद्यालय के शोधकर्ताओं ने हाइब्रिड क्वांटम-क्लासिकल बड़े भाषा मॉडल, HyQuT को विकसित किया, जिसमें प्राकृतिक भाषा निर्माण के लिए परिवर्तनीय क्वांटम सर्किट को ट्रांसफार्मर आर्किटेक्चर में एकीकृत किया गया।\n\nहाइब्रिड क्वांटम ट्रांसफॉर्मर भाषा निर्माण के लिए\n\nNovember 2, 2025\n\nCopy Markdown\n\nDesheng Kong, Xiangshuo Cui, Jiaying Jin, Jing Xu, Donglin Wang\n\n### सारांश\n\nनानकाई विश्वविद्यालय के शोधकर्ताओं ने हाइब्रिड क्वांटम-क्लासिकल बड़े भाषा मॉडल, HyQuT को विकसित किया, जिसमें प्राकृतिक भाषा निर्माण के लिए परिवर्तनीय क्वांटम सर्किट को ट्रांसफार्मर आर्किटेक्चर में एकीकृत किया गया। इस दृष्टिकोण ने 150 मिलियन मापदंडों तक के मॉडल में शास्त्रीय मापदंडों को 10% से अधिक कम कर दिया, साथ ही स्थिर प्रशिक्षण और सुसंगत पाठ निर्माण को बनाए रखा।\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n언어 생성을 위한 하이브리드 양자 트랜스포머 | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/ko/overview/2511.10653)\nciteturn4658search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; November 2, 2025 ... 난카이 대학교 연구원들은 자연어 생성을 위해 변분 양자 회로를 트랜스포머 아키텍처에 통합하여 최초의 하이브리드 양자-고전 대규모 언어 모델인 HyQuT를 개발했습니다. ... 난카이 대학교 연구원들은 자연어 생성을 위해 변분 양자 회로를 트랜스포머 아키텍처에 통합하여 최초의 하이브리드 양자-고전 대규모 언어 모델인 HyQuT를 개발했습니다.\n\n언어 생성을 위한 하이브리드 양자 트랜스포머\n\nNovember 2, 2025\n\nCopy Markdown\n\nDesheng Kong, Xiangshuo Cui, Jiaying Jin, Jing Xu, Donglin Wang\n\n### 요약\n\n난카이 대학교 연구원들은 자연어 생성을 위해 변분 양자 회로를 트랜스포머 아키텍처에 통합하여 최초의 하이브리드 양자-고전 대규모 언어 모델인 HyQuT를 개발했습니다. 이 접근 방식은 최대 1억 5천만 개의 파라미터를 가진 모델에서 고전적 파라미터를 10% 이상 감소시키면서 안정적인 훈련과 일관성 있는 텍스트 생성을 유지했습니다.\n\n난카이 대학교 연구원들은 자연어 생성을 위해 변분 양자 회로를 트랜스포머 아키텍처에 통합하여 최초의 하이브리드 양자-고전 대규모 언어 모델인 HyQuT를 개발했습니다. 이 접근 방식은 최대 1억 5천만 개의 파라미터를 가진 모델에서 고전적 파라미터를 10% 이상 감소시키면서 안정적인 훈련과 일관성 있는 텍스트 생성을 유지했습니다.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n混合量子变换器用于语言生成 | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/zh/overview/2511.10653)\nciteturn4658search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; November 2, 2025 ... 研究人员在两种规模下实现了 HyQuT：一个800万参数模型（HyQuT-8M）和一个1.5亿参数模型（HyQuT-150M）。\n\n混合量子变换器用于语言生成\n\nNovember 2, 2025\n\nCopy Markdown\n\nDesheng Kong, Xiangshuo Cui, Jiaying Jin, Jing Xu, Donglin Wang\n\n### AI 摘要\n\n南开大学研究人员通过将变分量子电路集成到Transformer架构中进行自然语言生成，开发了HyQuT，这是首个混合量子-经典大语言模型。这种方法使参数高达1.5亿的模型中的经典参数减少了10%以上，同时保持了稳定的训练和连贯的文本生成。\n\n南开大学研究人员通过将变分量子电路集成到Transformer架构中进行自然语言生成，开发了HyQuT，这是首个混合量子-经典大语言模型。这种方法使参数高达1.5亿的模型中的经典参数减少了10%以上，同时保持了稳定的训练和连贯的文本生成。\n\n  * 基于Transformer架构的大语言模型（LLMs）随着规模的扩大面临日益增长的计算和能源需求。\n  * 大多数现有的量子机器学习（QML）模型仅限于小规模的判别任务，缺乏与NLP领域大规模生成模型的集成。\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHybrider Quanten-Transformer für Sprachgenerierung | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/de/overview/2511.10653)\nciteturn4658search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; November 2, 2025 ... In dieser Arbeit stellen wir das erste hybride quantenklassische Large Language Model (LLM) für die natürliche Sprachgenerierung vor, HyQuT, das in der Lage ist, kohärente und kontextbewusste Dialoge zu führen.\n\nHybrider Quanten-Transformer für Sprachgenerierung\n\nNovember 2, 2025\n\nCopy Markdown\n\nDesheng Kong, Xiangshuo Cui, Jiaying Jin, Jing Xu, Donglin Wang\n\n### Zusammenfassung\n\nForscher der Nankai-Universität entwickelten HyQuT, das erste hybride quanten-klassische große Sprachmodell, indem sie variationale Quantenschaltungen in Transformer-Architekturen für die natürliche Spracherzeugung integrierten. Dieser Ansatz reduzierte die klassischen Parameter in Modellen mit bis zu 150 Millionen Parametern um über 10%, während das Training stabil blieb und eine kohärente Textgenerierung gewährleistet wurde.\n\nForscher der Nankai-Universität entwickelten HyQuT, das erste hybride quanten-klassische große Sprachmodell, indem sie variationale Quantenschaltungen in Transformer-Architekturen für die natürliche Spracherzeugung integrierten. Dieser Ansatz reduzierte die klassischen Parameter in Modellen mit bis zu 150 Millionen Parametern um über 10%, während das Training stabil blieb und eine kohärente Textgenerierung gewährleistet wurde.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOmid Abari's research works | University of California, Los Angeles and other places (https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Omid-Abari-2329902818)\nciteturn4658search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; November 2025 ... We present OmniVLA, an omni-modality VLA model that integrates novel sensing modalities for physically-grounded spatial intelligence beyond RGB perception.\nNovember 2025\n\n·\n\n43 Reads\n\nHeyu Guo\n\n·\n\nShanmu Wang\n\n·\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n·\n\n[...]\n\n·\n\nLili Qi\n\nVision-language-action (VLA) models have shown strong generalization for action prediction through large-scale vision-language pretraining. However, most existing models rely solely on RGB cameras, limiting their perception and, consequently, manipulation capabilities. We present OmniVLA, an omni-modality VLA model that integrates novel sensing modalities for physically-grounded spatial intelligence beyond RGB perception. The core of our approach is the sensor-masked image, a unified representation that overlays spatially grounded and physically meaningful masks onto the RGB images, derived from sensors including an infrared camera, a mmWave radar, and a microphone array. This image-native unification keeps sensor input close to RGB statistics to facilitate training, provides a uniform interface across sensor hardware, and enables data-efficient learning with lightweight per-sensor projectors. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOmid Abari's research works | University of California System, Oakland and other places (https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Omid-Abari-2044981906)\nciteturn4658search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; OmniVLA: Unifiying Multi-Sensor Perception for Physically-Grounded Multimodal VLA ... November 2025\n\nFile available\n\nNovember 2025\n\n·\n\n57 Reads\n\nHeyu Guo\n\n·\n\nShanmu Wang\n\n·\n\nRuichun Ma\n\n·\n\n[...]\n\n·\n\nLili Qi\n\nVision-language-action (VLA) models have shown strong generalization for action prediction through large-scale vision-language pretraining. However, most existing models rely solely on RGB cameras, limiting their perception and, consequently, manipulation capabilities. We present OmniVLA, an omni-modality VLA model that integrates novel sensing modalities for physically-grounded spatial intelligence beyond RGB perception. The core of our approach is the sensor-masked image, a unified representation that overlays spatially grounded and physically meaningful masks onto the RGB images, derived from sensors including an infrared camera, a mmWave radar, and a microphone array. This image-native unification keeps sensor input close to RGB statistics to facilitate training, provides a uniform interface across sensor hardware, and enables data-efficient learning with lightweight per-sensor projectors. Built on this, we present a multisensory vision-language-action model architecture and train the model based on an RGB-pretrained VLA backbone. We evaluate OmniVLA on challenging real-world tasks where sensor-modality perception is needed to guide the manipulation. OmniVLA achieves an average task success rate of 84%, significantly outperforms both RGB-only and raw-sensor-input baseline models by 59% and 28% respectively, meanwhile showing higher learning efficiency and stronger generalization capability.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHYBRID QUANTUM TRANSFORMER FOR LANGUAGE (https://www.znakschoola.ru/?_=%2Fpdf%2F2511.10653%23UE7DkG0PaBHZOakR54g1Wl8%3D)\nciteturn4658search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; tum–classical large language model (LLM) for natural language generation, HyQuT, capable of ... arXiv:2511.10653v1  [cs.CL]  2 Nov 2025\nHYBRID QUANTUM TRANSFORMER FOR LANGUAGE\nGENERATION ∗\nXiangshuo Cui\nNankai University\n{2120250604@mail.nankai.edu.cn}\nDesheng Kong\nNankai University\n{kongds@mail.nankai.edu.cn}\nJiaying Jin\nNankai University\n{2120250515@mail.nankai.edu.cn}\nJing Xu\nNankai University\n{xujing@nankai.edu.cn}\nDonglin Wang\nNankai University\nBeijing Sursen Information Technology Co., Ltd\n{wangdonglin@sursen.net}\nABSTRACT\nAlthough quantum computing has been increasingly applied to replace classical computation, most\nexisting quantum or hybrid models remain confined to simple tasks, with no successful application\nto large-scale natural language generation to date. In this work, we present the first hybrid quan-\ntum–classical large language model (LLM) for natural language generation, HyQuT, capable of\nperforming coherent and context-aware dialogue. The proposed architecture integrates variational\nquantum circuits (VQCs) into the Transformer framework at both 8M and 150M parameter scales.\nExperimental results show that a minimal number of qubits (10 qubits with 80 quantum gates)\ncan replace about 10% of the classical parameters in the 150M-parameter model, while achieving\ncomparable convergence stability and generation quality. This study provides an early demonstration\nof the feasibility of integrating quantum computing to large-scale generative language models.\nKeywords Quantum Transformer · Quantum machine learning · Large language models\n1\nIntroduction\narXiv:2511.10653v1  [cs.CL]  2 Nov 2025\nRecent advances in Transformer-based large language models (LLMs), beginning with the seminal Transformer\narchitecture[1], have driven remarkable progress in natural language generation. The paradigm of scaling these models,\nexemplified by landmark architectures like the GPT series[2, 3] and now widely adopted in open-source models such\nas LLaMA[4], has unlocked unprecedented capabilities. Yet, this continual scaling has led to substantial and often\nprohibitive computational and energy demands[5]. As model parameters grow into the hundreds of millions or billions,\ntraining and inference increasingly strain classical hardware resources, highlighting the urgent need for new computing\nparadigms to alleviate these bottlenecks. Quantum computing, with its potential for exponential parallelism and compact\ninformation representation, has emerged as a promising alternative for enhancing neural architectures[6].\nDespite rapid progress in quantum machine learning, most existing quantum or hybrid models remain limited to\nsmall-scale tasks such as classification, regression, or time-series forecasting. Their architectures typically involve\nshallow quantum circuits or isolated quantum layers without integration into large-scale generative models. To date, no\nstudy has successfully demonstrated a quantum–classical hybrid model capable of coherent and context-aware language\n∗Citation: Kong. HyQuT.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEuropean Patent Bulletin 2025/01 (https://www.epo.org/bulletin/downloads/2025/bulletin2501.pdf)\nciteturn4658search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.9 years ago; (A61K) II.1(1) — (01/2025) 01.01.2025 ... • PROCÉDÉS D'AMÉLIORATION DE L'IMMUNOGÉNICITÉ DE VACCINS SPÉCIFIQUES D'UN ANTIGÈNE FAIBLEMENT IMMUNOGÈNES À L'AIDE DE BÊTA-GLUCANES DE LEVURE ORAUX ... 12746721.5 / 2 585 084 ... (43) 28.09.2022 ... (73) Hyqut Molecule (Beijing) Technology Co., Ltd, Room 201-15, Building 13, Courtyard 53, Yanqi Avenue Yanqi Economic Development Zone Huirou District, Beijing 101407, CN\nA61K38/00 → (51) A61K38/17  \nA61K36/81 → (51) A24F40/42  \nA61K36/82 → (51) A61K31/353  \n\n(51) A61K38/00  \nA61P37/02  \nC07K14/715  \nC07K16/32  \nC07K14/54  \n(11) 3 885 357 B1  \nA61P37/04  \nC07K16/24  \nA61P35/00  \n\n(52) A61K38/00; A61P37/02; C07K14/715; C07K16/32; C07K14/54  \n(25) Zh  \n(26) En  \n(21) 19886303.7  \n(22) 18.11.2019  \n(84) AL AT BE BG CH CY CZ DE DK EE ES FI FR GB GR HR HU IE IS IT LI LT LU LV MC MK MT NL NO PL PT RO RS SE SI SK SM TR  \n(43) 29.09.2021  \n(86) CN 2019/119088 18.11.2019  \n(87) WO 2020/103777 2020/22 28.05.2020  \n(30) 22.11.2018 CN 201811400000  \n(54) • INTERLEUKIN 21-PROTEIN (IL21)-MUTANTE UND VERWENDUNG DAVON  \n• INTERLEUKIN 21 PROTEIN (IL21) MUTANT AND USE THEREOF  \n• MUTANT DE LA PROTÉINE INTERLEUKINE 21 (IL21) ET SON UTILISATION  \n(73) Hyqut Molecule (Beijing) Technology Co., Ltd, Room 201-15, Building 13, Courtyard 53, Yanqi Avenue Yanqi Economic Development Zone H